{"archetypes":[{"name":"sanitization-tracer","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's primary IP-leakage risk is that consumer-repo data reaches a public larch issue; the static panel won't trace every composition path through the allowlist versus the test deny-list.","prompt_body":"Trace every data path from `$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/ship-pr-state.sh`, `execution-issues.md`, `session-env.sh`, and the `--failure-detail-log` path into the composed `bug-body` and `bug-comment` outputs, verifying the allowlist enumerated in `stall-recovery-report.md` fully covers all proposed fields with no bypass route. Check whether the test-harness deny-list assertions in `test-stall-recovery-report.sh` actually exercise the same fields enumerated in `stall-recovery-report.md`, rather than ad-hoc strings that could miss newly added fields. Verify that `redact-secrets.sh` is invoked after allowlist assembly (not before), so a field passing the allowlist but containing a secret-like substring is still caught. Confirm the consumer-repo chat-print branch uses the same `bug-body` subcommand rather than a separate, unguarded body-assembly path. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"state-rewrite-auditor","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The success path's correctness hinges on STALL_TRACKING=false being persisted to ship-pr-state.sh before Step 18 reads it; the plan describes this only at a sketch level and the static panel won't audit the write-order and crash-safety constraints.","prompt_body":"Examine every point in the plan where `STALL_TRACKING` is read or written, checking that the proposed key-based rewrite of `ship-pr-state.sh` on the success path is specified precisely enough (write-to-temp-then-mv or equivalent) to avoid leaving a partially truncated state file on a mid-write crash. Verify the plan unambiguously orders the in-memory clear and the on-disk persist so that Step 18 teardown reads `STALL_TRACKING=false` after a successful recovery, not a stale `true`. Check that `stall-recovery-attempts.env` is initialized before the first retry iteration rather than lazily, so the retry counter is reliable if the recovery gate exits abruptly mid-loop. Confirm the plan's same-cause-repeat detection reads `FAILURE_SIGNATURE` from the prior attempt's persisted record rather than from in-memory state that a crash would lose. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"cross-contract-sync","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan spreads the interface across three new files (stall-recovery-report.sh, stall-recovery-report.md, stall-recovery.md) plus SKILL.md; subcommand names, exit codes, RESUME_HINT tokens, and retry caps must agree exactly across all four surfaces and the static panel won't do cross-document symbol matching.","prompt_body":"Check that every subcommand name (`classify`, `is-larch-dev-clone`, `bug-body`, `bug-comment`, `issue-input-file`) appears consistently across `stall-recovery-report.sh`, `stall-recovery-report.md`, and `references/stall-recovery.md`, and that the exit-code contract (0/1/2/3) is documented identically in both prose documents. Verify that the retry caps listed in `stall-recovery-report.md` match the caps referenced in `references/stall-recovery.md`, and that the plan designates one as the authoritative source so they cannot silently diverge. Check that the `RESUME_HINT` token set emitted by `classify` exactly matches the `switch` dispatch arms in `references/stall-recovery.md`, with no token that appears in one but lacks a corresponding case in the other. Confirm the `LARCH_STALL_RECOVERY_DRY_RUN=1` testing knob is documented in `stall-recovery-report.md` and that the test harness exercises it with an assertion, not merely mentions it. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
